- name: note_try
  id: note
  parameters:
    note: "Three things to try, in order.\n\n1. WITH TWO ANTENNAS, find any steady carrier\
      \ and watch coherence. Move one\n   antenna a few centimetres and the angle moves; put\
      \ it back and the angle\n   comes back. That repeatability IS the coherent-receiver\
      \ property.\n\n2. TICK `zero`, then move an antenna. The reading is now relative to\
      \ where you\n   zeroed. Untick it to see the raw angle again - the raw number is on\
      \ its own\n   readout precisely so that zeroing can never hide it.\n\n3. WIDEN `band-select`\
      \ past the LO offset, so that DC falls inside the filter.\n   Coherence will climb toward\
      \ 1 and stay there, steady and convincing, and it\n   will be measuring the receiver's\
      \ own LO leak talking to itself. This is the\n   failure this example is arranged to\
      \ avoid, and it is worth seeing once so\n   you recognise it elsewhere.\n\nThe averaging\
      \ control is a trade: more frames is a steadier angle and a slower\nresponse to a real\
      \ change. At the default chunk of 4096 samples and 8 frames,\nthe estimate settles in\
      \ a few tenths of a second."
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 8
    - 720
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
